From bcd1dbcbb98198052c95ec99860ade75b94e0bdd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 17:24:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06926/11362] [outer-loop] g50t: L7 mapped, unverified
 candidate is a degenerate frame (round 11)

Round-11 gpt-5.6-sol session made real progress mapping L7: two paired
color-15 swap sockets (left pair activated by the autonomous runner,
right pair requiring phase synchronization with a remote plate), a
color-8 gate plate, and a distinct L7-internal action clock separate
from the session budget. The session proposed a compact 43-action
candidate tail, explicitly flagged as an untested hypothesis for
outer-loop verification, not a claimed win.

The outer loop tested it directly: the full 331-action sequence
reaches state=GameState.WIN, but with levels_completed=0, win_levels=0,
and an entirely empty frame (shape (0,)) -- none of which match the
pattern of every genuine win banked this session (always
levels_completed == achieved level, normally-populated frame).
Stepping back one action shows level=6, NOT_FINISHED, normal frame --
only the single final action triggers this. This is almost certainly
an environment-level artifact (an action-limit or gateway-exhaustion
sentinel), not a genuine completion, and is not banked as a win.

No new level banked; frontier stays at level 6. Next attempt should
isolate the final few actions individually rather than trusting this
exact tail, and continue mapping the right-pair phase sync toward a
real win.

